<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- RELEASE entitlements. Identical to App.entitlements except aps-environment,
	     which must be "production" here: distribution builds are signed MANUALLY
	     against the "SwiftCard App Store" profile, and that profile grants
	     aps-environment=production. A mismatch fails the archive outright — which
	     is the point. Debug keeps App.entitlements (development) for device builds
	     signed with a development profile.

	     Why this file exists at all: builds used to archive with
	     CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, which skips the step that compiles a .xcent from
	     CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS. exportArchive then signed the app with only the
	     entitlements it could infer (application-identifier, team-identifier), so
	     shipped builds carried NO aps-environment, NO app group and NO associated
	     domains even though the profile granted all three. Push registration
	     failed on every device with "no valid aps-environment entitlement string",
	     Universal Links opened Safari, and the widget could not read its shared
	     container. scripts/ios-release.sh now signs the archive and verifies the
	     exported binary's real entitlements before it will upload.

	     NO associated domains, on purpose (owner, 2026-09-29): no swiftcard.me
	     link may ever open this app. See App.entitlements. The release script
	     now refuses to upload a build that carries them. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.me.swiftcard.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
